{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790366192,"nonce":"YJ1t43BgpM79rWoP9tEzj8sH8aw=","title":"Windows: the interpreter's typed extern call refuses mixed integer/float arguments","message":"CI run 36165267706 on 14ac211c, native tests (x86_64-pc-windows-msvc): zyntax_compiler's lib test hir_interp::tests::typed_extern_uses_float_registers_for_mixed_arguments_and_return fails with UnsupportedInstruction(\"mixed integer/float extern ABI on Windows\"). The typed extern call packs integer and float arguments into two register sequences, which is right on System V and AArch64 but not on Windows x64, which assigns registers by position; it refused every mixed call there. The JIT dispatch (call_jit_dispatch) had the same per-class packing with no refusal, so a JIT entry whose float argument precedes an integer one got its arguments in the wrong registers.\n\nFixed on main by 4fa12dab: both go through a positional dispatcher on Windows (the first four arguments by their own class, later ones as 8-byte stack words), with a Windows-only test of six interleaved arguments. Compiles and passes clippy for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc from the Mac; unit tests pass on the Mac. To close once Windows CI passes.","files":null}]}